/*
Problem: Valid Anagram
Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-anagram/

Approach:
- If the lengths of both strings are different, they cannot be anagrams.
- Traverse the first string.
- For each character, find its first occurrence in the second string.
- If found, erase that character from the second string.
- If not found, return false.
- If all characters are removed from the second string, the strings are anagrams.

Mistake & Learning:
- Initially, I called t.find(s[i]) twice: once to check if the character existed and again while erasing it.
- Learned that storing the returned index in a variable avoids repeating the same search.
- Learned how to use:
    - string::find() → Returns the index of the first occurrence of a character/string, or string::npos if not found.
    - string::erase(pos, count) → Removes 'count' characters starting from index 'pos'.
*/

class Solution {
public:
    bool isAnagram(string s, string t) {
        int n = s.size();
        int m = t.size();

        if (n != m) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int pos = t.find(s[i]);

            if (pos == string::npos) {
                return false;
            }

            t.erase(pos, 1);
        }

        return t.empty();
    }
};

/*
Time Complexity: O(n²)
Space Complexity: O(1)

Possible Optimization:
- Use a frequency array (size 26) or an unordered_map to achieve O(n) time complexity.
*/
